  <h1>Privacy Policy – Atlas Networks FiveM API</h1>
  <p>Effective Date: May 3, 2025 • Last Updated: May 3, 2025</p>
</header>

<main>
  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>This Privacy Policy outlines how the Atlas Networks FiveM API bot (the “Bot”) accesses and handles user data. This bot connects Discord and FiveM platforms to enforce permissions and synchronize user status. It is built using the open-source project <a href="https://github.com/JaredScar/Badger_Discord_API" target="_blank">Badger_Discord_API</a> by JaredScar, and used in compliance with its license.</p>

  <h2>2. What Data is Accessed</h2>
  <p>The Bot accesses the following Discord information during a user’s active session in the FiveM server:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Discord Username and Discriminator</li>
    <li>Discord User ID</li>
    <li>Assigned Discord Roles</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This data is accessed temporarily to verify permissions, enforce in-game rules, and facilitate integration between the Discord server and the FiveM server.</p>

  <h2>3. No Data Storage</h2>
  <p>The Bot does <strong>not</strong> permanently store, log, or archive any user data. All data access occurs in real-time while the user is connected to the server, and is discarded after the session ends.</p>

  <h2>4. Infrastructure Security</h2>
  <p>The Bot is configured to interact only with pre-approved components of the Atlas Networks infrastructure. Any attempt to use the Bot to gain access to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Atlas configuration files</li>
    <li>Root server environments</li>
    <li>Internal dashboards or administrative systems</li>
  </ul>
  <p>is strictly prohibited and may result in removal from all Atlas platforms and potential escalation.</p>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Code Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>This Bot is based on code created by <a href="https://github.com/JaredScar/Badger_Discord_API" target="_blank">JaredScar</a>. All rights, licensing terms, and credits for that project are acknowledged and honored by Atlas Networks. We do not claim ownership of the underlying API framework.</p>

  <h2>6. Policy Updates</h2>
  <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated to reflect changes in how the Bot operates or how data is accessed. Any such changes will be reflected on this page. Continued use of the Bot constitutes acceptance of the current policy.</p>
</main>

